From f285b76e7d455d7ecfde67a58c3d59f166f99720 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: greyoak111 <151205158+greyoak111@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:33:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 45/48] Check for and install updates from GitHub Releases

A new Updates tab: automatic mode (default) checks shortly after launch
and every six hours, downloads a newer release in the background and
installs it when LiveHime quits; manual mode checks and downloads only on
request through the same path. A download is kept only when its SHA-256
matches the release's digest and the app inside has this app's bundle id,
the release's version and a valid signature by the same certificate, so
permissions carry over. Installing waits for LiveHime to quit, swaps the
bundle (restoring the old one if that fails) and can reopen it; "Restart
and update" is refused while streaming or recording. A banner above the
tabs announces a found or downloaded version. Development builds only
point to the releases page.

Test hooks: Update (drive the tab) and Snapshot (render the dock to PNG);
e2e-update.mjs covers checksum and signer rejection and a full automatic
update and relaunch against a local feed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
