+## Updates
+
+`e2e-update.mjs` runs the updater against a local release feed
+(`LIVEHIME_UPDATE_FEED`), with no GitHub or real account involved. It copies
+the built app to `<work dir>/install`, builds a 9.9.9 variant signed like the
+build and another signed ad hoc, and checks that a download failing its
+digest and the ad hoc app are both discarded, then that automatic mode
+downloads and verifies 9.9.9 and "restart" quits LiveHime, swaps the bundle
+and reopens it at 9.9.9 with a valid signature (still on the e2e keychain):
+
+```bash
+node e2e-update.mjs <websocket password> build_macos/frontend/RelWithDebInfo/LiveHime.app /tmp/livehime-update
+```
+
+Afterwards remove `~/Library/Caches/local.livehime.macos.dev/Updates`.
+The `Snapshot` vendor request renders the dock (optionally a tab) to a PNG,
+for checking layouts without screen recording permission.
+
 ## Cover manager check
 
 `e2e-cover.mjs` drives Bilibili's cover manager in the real window: a real
